  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "The point of intersection <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> of the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and the line joining the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> divides the line segment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> internally in the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>|</mo></math> are coprime) are the direction ratios of the perpendicular from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math> on the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to _____ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "10",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>Plane: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now equation of line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>10</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p>Any point on line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now using perpendicular condition to find the point of intersection of line and plane,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So, point of intersection will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#956;</mi></math></p><p>Now any point on the line&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>&nbsp;is given by,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/6cb6575d-50c4-4bd9-98db-e57b68da818c-9896844.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 166px;\" /></p><p>Now direction ratio of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Now again using the perpendicular condition we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>14</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>11</mn><mn>14</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>42</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>130</mn></mrow><mn>42</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>85</mn><mn>42</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now on simplifying the Direction ratios we get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>42</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>130</mn></mrow><mn>42</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>85</mn><mn>42</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>26</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>17</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now on comparing with&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;we get,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>.</p>",
